\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Variance decomposition (Henderson Method~I) across five benchmarks and eight models. Multiple-choice benchmarks share an item-dominated structure; HellaSwag is the exception where model$\times $item (36.0\%) exceeds item difficulty (34.3\%). Free-form benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH) distribute variance across item, model, and interaction components with no single dominant source.}}{7}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cross_benchmark}{{8}{7}{Variance decomposition (Henderson Method~I) across five benchmarks and eight models. Multiple-choice benchmarks share an item-dominated structure; HellaSwag is the exception where model$\times $item (36.0\%) exceeds item difficulty (34.3\%). Free-form benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH) distribute variance across item, model, and interaction components with no single dominant source}{figure.caption.21}{}}
